    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0608" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/240</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-09T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 9, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3652. Department advised that British S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Barbara</hi>,
                    with Americans on board, was sunk by a German submarine in the British Channel
                    October 20. The vessel was carrying cargo of coal from Philadelphia to
                    Hartlepool.</p>
                <p>Please request the Foreign Minister for prompt investigation and report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
